From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 13] i915: the VBT from the ACPI OpRegion without CONFIG_ACPI

The illumos build has no CONFIG_ACPI and so no intel_opregion.c:
intel_opregion_get_vbt() returns NULL, the PCI ROM holds no VBT on a
UEFI boot, and i915 would run on its "VBT missing" defaults. The VBT
brings the panel, spread-spectrum and port data Linux uses.
intel_bios_get_vbt() asks drivers/i915/illumos/i915_illumos_vbt.c after
the OpRegion, which copies the VBT out of the OpRegion (RVDA/RVDS or
mailbox 4, validated with intel_bios_is_valid_vbt()) without writing to
it, and returns a kmalloc() copy as intel_opregion_get_vbt() does.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_bios.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_bios.c
@@ -3222,6 +3222,11 @@
 	intel_rom_free(rom);
 	return NULL;
 }
+
+#ifdef __illumos__
+/* drivers/i915/illumos/i915_illumos_vbt.c */
+#include "i915_illumos_vbt.h"
+#endif
 
 static const struct vbt_header *intel_bios_get_vbt(struct intel_display *display,
 						   size_t *sizep)
@@ -3232,6 +3237,12 @@
 
 	if (!vbt)
 		vbt = intel_opregion_get_vbt(display, sizep);
+
+#ifdef __illumos__
+	/* The OpRegion's VBT without CONFIG_ACPI, read-only. */
+	if (!vbt)
+		vbt = i915_illumos_opregion_vbt(display, sizep);
+#endif
 
 	/*
 	 * If the OpRegion does not have VBT, look in SPI flash
